# APIM MCP ↔ Azure DevOps OBO Flow — REST Client test file
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prerequisites:
#   • VS Code extension: REST Client (humao.rest-client)
#   • Either:
#       a) Set @bearerToken below manually (run tools/test-auth.ps1 and paste), OR
#       b) Use the az CLI snippet at the bottom to get a token automatically
#
# Usage:
#   Click "Send Request" above any ### block to run that request.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@gateway        = https://apim-mcp-ado-mcp-ado.azure-api.net
@apimClientId   = 355d2574-1ed9-4fa3-9197-8de6242f8412
@tenantId       = 1318d57f-757b-45b3-b1b0-9b3c3842774f
@apimScope      = api://{{apimClientId}}/user_impersonation

# Paste a token here (or generate one with the device-code request below)
@bearerToken    = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

###
# ── 1. Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728) ─────────────────────────────────
# Verifies the PRM endpoint returns correct OAuth resource metadata.
# Expected: 200 with resource, authorization_servers, scopes_supported
GET {{gateway}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

###
# ── 2. MCP endpoint — no token (expect 401 + WWW-Authenticate) ───────────────
POST {{gateway}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "initialize",
  "id": 1,
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "rest-client", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

###
# ── 3. MCP initialize — with Bearer token ─────────────────────────────────────
# Expected:
#   200  — OBO succeeded, forwarded to ADO MCP backend
#   403  — consent_required; open {{gateway}}/authorize in a browser
#   401  — token invalid / expired; get a new token
POST {{gateway}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "initialize",
  "id": 1,
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "rest-client", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

###
# ── 4. MCP tools/list — after successful initialize ───────────────────────────
POST {{gateway}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "tools/list",
  "id": 2
}

###
# ── 5. Consent redirect (open in browser, not REST Client) ────────────────────
# If request 3 returns 403 consent_required, visit this URL in a browser.
# After granting consent, retry request 3.
GET {{gateway}}/authorize

###
# ── 6. Device code — start (get user_code + verification_uri) ─────────────────
# Run this to bootstrap a token without running test-auth.ps1.
# Then open verification_uri in a browser and enter user_code.
# Finally run request 7 with the device_code from the response.
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{apimClientId}}&scope={{apimScope}} openid profile

###
# ── 7. Device code — poll for token ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Replace DEVICE_CODE with the value returned by request 6.
# Poll every ~5 s until you get access_token (authorization_pending is normal).
# Copy the access_token value into @bearerToken above.
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{apimClientId}}&grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code&device_code=DEVICE_CODE
